  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Intaglio Note",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Intaglio Note\"**\n\nThe market is a sheet of security-printed currency. Every hero surface is a banknote face: a deep intaglio-green field with a double engraved frame, a guilloche rosette seeded by the coin it represents, a wave band whose lines literally trace the price series, a copper serial number, and a microprint rule along the bottom edge. Everything around the notes is the paper they are printed on: cool cotton-rag neutrals, hairline rules, and a quiet ledger of tabular numbers.\n\nDensity is a trading ledger, not a dashboard of cards. The market table, movers list, and supply data are plain rows on paper separated by hairlines; panels exist only to group a tool (chart, converter, supply). Ornament is generated from live data and never drawn as decoration for its own sake: the rosette is seeded from a coin's id, the band from Bitcoin's 24h sparkline, the serial from a hash of the coin. Numbers are the hero, set in wide, heavy Archivo like a note's denomination.\n\nThe world explicitly refuses the neon-on-black glass crypto dashboard: no glows, no gradients-as-brand, no glassy cards. Dark mode is the same note printed on night paper, not a different aesthetic.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Two materials only: paper (neutral surfaces, ledger rows) and note (green intaglio field for heroes and the one active choice in a control).",
      "Guilloche, microprint and serials are procedurally generated from real data.",
      "One variable family, Archivo, used at three widths: 125 for denominations, 100 for UI, 85 for serials.",
      "Gain/loss always carries sign and arrow alongside green/oxblood.",
      "Flat paper; only notes, dialogs and solid buttons lift."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Direction-Only Rule",
        "body": "Up and down colours mean price direction and nothing else, and they never appear without a sign and an arrow.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Note Rule",
        "body": "Intaglio Green fills at most one hero surface per screen plus the single selected item of a control. Panels, cards and rows are paper.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Copper Thread Rule",
        "body": "Copper marks identity and attention (serials, active indicator, focus ring, starred state) as a thin line or glyph, never as a background.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Three Widths Rule",
        "body": "Width encodes role: 125 is money, 100 is language, 85 is a code. Do not set prose wide or prices condensed.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "Every number on screen uses tabular lining figures so columns and live updates never jitter.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Paper Rule",
        "body": "Panels, rows, chips and inputs carry a hairline border and no shadow. If it is printed on the paper, it does not float.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** render every hero as a note: Intaglio Green field, double inner frame, data-seeded rosette, copper serial, microprint edge.",
      "**Do** derive ornament from data: seed rosettes with the coin id, trace guilloche bands from a real price series, hash serials from the coin.",
      "**Do** pair every gain/loss colour with a sign and an up/down-right arrow, and give it screen-reader text.",
      "**Do** set money in denomination type (Archivo wdth 125, 800) and every number in tabular figures.",
      "**Do** keep panels flat on paper with 1px hairlines and 14px corners; reserve the Note and Lift shadows for notes, dialogs and solid buttons.",
      "**Do** use the copper ring (2px, offset 2px) for all keyboard focus.",
      "**Do** collapse table columns progressively on small screens instead of turning rows into cards.",
      "**Do** honour reduced motion: the global override flattens all animation and transition durations."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** build neon-on-black glass dashboards: no glows, glassy translucent cards, or gradient brand fills.",
      "**Don't** use up/down green or oxblood for buttons, brand, links or decoration.",
      "**Don't** fill more than one hero surface per screen with Intaglio Green.",
      "**Don't** put information in microprint; it is aria-hidden texture at 5.5px.",
      "**Don't** introduce a second typeface or a monospace; use Archivo's width axis and tabular figures.",
      "**Don't** use copper as a background fill or for body text.",
      "**Don't** add drop shadows to panels, rows, chips or inputs."
    ]
  }
}